    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered account of what happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is served entirely by an OfficeFloor pipeline defined in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (there is **no** Spring `@RestController` \u2014 the only `@PostMapping` is an unimplemented generated OpenAPI interface).\n\nTwo things worth flagging up front:\n- **The DTO bean-validation annotations (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Email`, `@Size` on `OwnerFieldsDto`) never fire.** Step 3 binds `@RequestBody` *without* `@Valid`, so all validation is done manually by the pipeline steps instead.\n- **Steps 1\u20137 run outside the transaction; steps 8\u201318 run under `govern: [ transaction ]`**, committing once at the end.\n\n## Validations & side-effects, in execution order\n\n**0. Authorization (gate).** `composition: authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` guards the whole endpoint. Denial \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 **403**.\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key was seen before, throws `IdempotentReplayException` carrying the stored owner \u2192 short-circuits to **200** (a replay, not an error).\n\n**2. `RequireDailyLimit`** \u2014 counts owners registered today (business-day-adjusted); if `>= 100`, throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n**3. `RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 *the only `@RequestBody` binding.* Side-effect: computes and writes back the effective address (normalized `addressLine1[+addressLine2]`, else the flat `address`). Validation: requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**. Publishes `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`.\n\n**4. `RequireValidPostcode`** \u2014 if a postcode is present, it must be 4 digits and fall in the region range for the city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**5. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 side-effect: rewrites telephone to E.164 (strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps `+`, else assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`). Validation: result must be 8\u201315 digits \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**6. `ValidateTelephoneCountryLength`** \u2014 `+61` requires 9 national digits, `+1` requires 10 \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**7. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 if email present: side-effect lower-cases it in place; validation requires it match the email regex and not be a disposable domain (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n*\u2014 transaction begins here \u2014*\n\n**8. `RequireUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 computes `identityKey` = SHA-256 of `telephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`; if a non-deleted owner already has it, throws `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**9. `RequireCityCapacity`** \u2014 if the city already holds `>= 50` owners (case-insensitive), throws `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n**10. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`. Validation: rejects a future `registrationDate` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**. Side-effect: defaults `registrationDate` to today and rolls it to the next business day (skips weekends/2026 holidays). Publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n**11. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 side-effect: sets `memberId` = `V2<REGION><FY><HASH8><Luhn-check>`; on collision appends `-<n>`.\n\n**12. `CountNamesakes`** \u2014 side-effect: sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**13. `CountHousehold`** \u2014 side-effect: sets `householdCount` = existing household members (last name + postcode) + 1.\n\n**14. `FlagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 side-effect: if not `sharesHousehold`, sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a soundex(lastName)+postcode match with a *different* identityKey exists.\n\n**15. `CapMembershipLevel`** \u2014 side-effect: caps `membershipLevel` at (highest household member's level + 1), otherwise the natural level.\n\n**16. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 side-effect: `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (the persistence write).\n\n**17. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 side-effect: if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, stores the saved owner's DTO in the `IdempotencyStore`.\n\n**18. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 side-effects: computes a `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 owners created today), writes AUDIT + NOTIFY log entries, and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Summary\n\n- **Validations (in order):** auth `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2192 idempotency replay check \u2192 daily limit (<100) \u2192 required fields \u2192 postcode format/region \u2192 telephone E.164 length \u2192 telephone country-specific length \u2192 email syntax/non-disposable \u2192 unique identity key \u2192 city capacity (<50) \u2192 registration date not in the future.\n- **Side-effects (in order):** address composed & written back \u2192 telephone rewritten to E.164 \u2192 email lower-cased \u2192 owner built + registrationDate defaulted/rolled to a business day \u2192 `memberId` assigned \u2192 `namesakeCount` set \u2192 `householdCount` set \u2192 `possibleDuplicate` flags set \u2192 `membershipLevel` capped \u2192 persisted \u2192 idempotency key recorded \u2192 audit/notify logs + bulk-signup warning + 201 with Location header.\n\nNote the transaction boundary: any failure in steps 8\u201318 rolls back the whole thing, whereas the string mutations in steps 3/5/7 happen before the transaction (they only mutate the in-memory DTO, so that's harmless)."
